\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Linear Gaussian SSM: state RMSE (lower is better), common threshold $0.5N$. Resample when $E_2=1/\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _iw_i^2$, $E_H=\exp (-\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _iw_i\log w_i)$ or $E_\infty =1/\max _iw_i$ falls below $0.5N$. $E_\infty \le E_2\le E_H$, so $E_\infty $ resamples most often and $E_H$ least. $CV^2>1$ is the same rule as $E_2<0.5N$. 50 steps; 100 filter runs over 10 observation sequences (10 for OT and Gumbel).}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:trigger-fixed-linear-rmse}{{1}{1}{}{}{}}
